34 must be before CS4215, so ST2334 in Sem 6 or 7. Sem 6 is exchange (0 MC), so ST2334 cannot be in Sem 6. So ST2334 in Sem 7. Then CS2102 in Sem 7. CS2102 offered Sem 1,2. Sem 7 is Sem 1. OK. CS3242 requires CS3241 and PC1201. CS3241 offered Sem 1. CS3242 offered Sem 2. CS3241 must be before CS3242. CS3241 can be in Sem 6 (exchange, no) or Sem 7 (full) or Sem 8 (full). If CS3241 in Sem 7, Sem 7 has CS2102, ST2334, CS3241. 3 modules. OK. PC1201 must be before CS3242. PC1201 offered Sem 1,2. Can be in Sem 6 (no), Sem 7 (full), Sem 8 (full). If PC1201 in Sem 7, Sem 7 has 4 modules. Limit 3. No. If PC1201 in Sem 8, Sem 8 has CS4215, CS3236, CS3242, PC1201. 4 modules. Limit 3. No. If PC1201 in Sem 5? Student is in Sem 6. Cannot go back. So PC1201 must be in Sem 6, 7, or 8. Sem 6 is exchange. Sem 7 and 8 are full. We cannot fit PC1201 and CS3241 and CS3242 and CS4215 and CS3236 and CS2102 and ST2334 in Sem 7 and 8 with limit 3. Sem 7: CS2102, ST2334. Sem 8: CS4215, CS3236, CS3242. CS3241 and PC1201 must be taken before CS3242. They must be in Sem 6 (no) or earlier. Student is in Sem 6. Cannot take in Sem 5. So impossible.",
    "PC1201 and CS3241 are prerequisites for CS3242. CS3242 is offered in Sem 2. CS3241 is offered in Sem 1. The student is in Sem 6 (Y3S2). Sem 6 is exchange (0 MC). Sem 7 is Y4S1 (Sem 1). Sem 8 is Y4S2 (Sem 2). CS3241 must be taken in Sem 6 or earlier to be before CS3242 in Sem 8? No, CS3241 can be in Sem 7 (Sem 1) and CS3242 in Sem 8 (Sem 2). But Sem 7 is full with CS2102 and ST2334. Adding CS3241 makes 3. Then PC1201 must be taken. PC1201 can be in Sem 7? No, 4 modules. PC1201 in Sem 8? Sem 8 has CS4215, CS3236, CS3242. Adding PC1201 makes 4. No. PC1201 in Sem 6? Exchange, 0 MC. No. So PC1201 cannot be taken. Thus CS3242 cannot be taken.",
    "Even if PC1201 was not required, CS3241 in Sem 7 and CS3242 in Sem 8 works for prerequisites. But PC1201 is required. And PC1201 cannot be scheduled."
  ]
}

